---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
import EngagementContact from '../components/EngagementContact.astro';
import {engagementSteps,responsibilities,reporting} from '../data/engagement';
import {commercialQuestions,accessQuestions} from '../data/commercial';
import ReviewNote from '../components/ReviewNote.astro';
---
<Marketing title="How we work" description="A non-custodial service mandate: agree the markets, capital, permissions and operating limits, then follow activity through the client dashboard.">
 <section class="service-hero work-hero"><p class="section-kicker">How we work</p><h1>A clear mandate.<br/>A visible operation.</h1><div class="service-lead"><p>Agree the work before it starts. Retain control of your assets and follow the activity through the client dashboard.</p><a class="home-button" href="#contact">Discuss your mandate</a></div></section>
 <section class="work-process" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="section-intro"><h2 id="process-title">From first review<br/>to ongoing operation.</h2><p>Each engagement is scoped around<br/>the client and market.</p></div><ol>{engagementSteps.map(step=><li><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
 <section id="responsibilities" class="responsibility-section" aria-labelledby="responsibility-title"><div class="section-intro"><h2 id="responsibility-title">Who controls what.</h2><p>Non-custodial access.<br/>Defined responsibilities.</p></div><table class="responsibility-table"><caption>Responsibilities within the agreed service mandate</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Your team</th><th scope="col">Onchain Bureau</th></tr></thead><tbody>{responsibilities.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.area}</th><td>{row.client}</td><td>{row.bureau}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p class="operating-note">Exchanges and protocols provide the underlying trading environment. Their availability and behaviour are dependencies considered when defining the mandate.</p></section>
 <section id="review" class="work-review editorial-section" aria-labelledby="review-title"><div class="editorial-intro"><p class="section-kicker">Operation and review</p><h2 id="review-title">Visibility throughout<br/>the engagement.</h2><p>The live client dashboard lets you inspect activity and review liquidity against your agreed SLA. Reporting coverage, communication and review arrangements are defined for the markets in scope.</p></div><dl class="review-capabilities">{reporting.map(item=><div><dt>{item.title}</dt><dd>{item.text}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
 <section id="commercials" class="work-terms editorial-section" aria-labelledby="terms-title"><div><p class="section-kicker">The commercial model</p><h2 id="terms-title">Your capital.<br/>A service fee.<br/>Clear economics.</h2><p>You supply the liquidity capital. Onchain Bureau manages the scoped activity for an agreed fee. The fee and capital requirement depend on the engagement.</p><p>Before committing, settle four questions:</p></div><dl class="decision-list">{commercialQuestions.map(item=><div><dt>{item.title}</dt><dd>{item.text}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
 <ReviewNote title="Make commercial qualification concrete" items={['Confirm fee structure, practical minimum engagement/capital, typical scope and contract duration.','Confirm allocation of P&L, rebates, LP fees and operating costs, plus termination and withdrawal mechanics. No default economics are assumed.']}/>
 <section id="controls" class="control-section editorial-section" aria-labelledby="control-title"><div><p class="section-kicker">Access and operating boundaries</p><h2 id="control-title">Define authority<br/>before operation.</h2><p>Non-custodial access describes who retains control of the assets. The permission configuration and operating procedures determine what can happen within the engagement.</p><p>Use these questions to establish the setup before access is enabled.</p></div><dl class="decision-list">{accessQuestions.map(item=><div><dt>{item.title}</dt><dd>{item.text}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
 <ReviewNote title="Document the actual controls" items={['Supply the approved CEX API actions and Safe/Squads roles, including revocation and emergency pause authority.','Confirm monitoring coverage, named escalation roles, incident procedure and restart approval. Do not infer withdrawal restrictions, 24/7 human coverage or automatic safeguards.']}/>
 <section class="starting-brief" aria-labelledby="starting-title"><h2 id="starting-title">Bring us your market.</h2><div><p>For the first conversation, share:</p><ul><li>Your token and project website</li><li>Existing or planned exchanges, pairs and pools</li><li>Your current liquidity setup and an indicative capital range, if known</li><li>What you want to improve, and any timing constraints</li></ul><p>The initial discussion establishes the proposed scope, capital needs and access requirements. It is also the time to confirm venue support and the people responsible for the work.</p><p>No API keys or account access are needed to start that conversation.</p></div></section>
 <EngagementContact subject="Service mandate enquiry"/>
</Marketing>
